{"slug":"student-attendance-record-ii","title":"Student Attendance Record II","level":"Hard","summary":"Records of length n use A (absent), L (late) and P (present). Count the records with fewer than 2 A in total and never 3 or more consecutive L, modulo 10^9 + 7.","method":"checkRecord","params":[["int","n"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["2"],"out":"8"},{"in":["1"],"out":"3"},{"in":["10101"],"out":"183236316"},{"in":["3"],"out":"19"},{"in":["100"],"out":"985598218"},{"in":["4049"],"out":"798495319","g":1},{"in":["4"],"out":"43","g":1},{"in":["27261"],"out":"398521913","g":1},{"in":["38853"],"out":"127169846","g":1},{"in":["72097"],"out":"547493770","g":1},{"in":["74266"],"out":"242118564","g":1},{"in":["85904"],"out":"912321535","g":1},{"in":["33352"],"out":"478562744","g":1},{"in":["47159"],"out":"826674370","g":1},{"in":["40478"],"out":"188052488","g":1},{"in":["4428"],"out":"755115906","g":1},{"in":["36662"],"out":"889991258","g":1},{"in":["10"],"out":"3536","g":1},{"in":["59183"],"out":"88125007","g":1},{"in":["100000"],"out":"749184020","g":1},{"in":["93552"],"out":"408995530","g":1},{"in":["68039"],"out":"138421567","g":1},{"in":["99868"],"out":"348922494","g":1},{"in":["79722"],"out":"612531966","g":1},{"in":["86429"],"out":"275198234","g":1},{"in":["70759"],"out":"199928413","g":1},{"in":["79849"],"out":"570369506","g":1},{"in":["50032"],"out":"857384401","g":1},{"in":["11939"],"out":"821576399","g":1},{"in":["25539"],"out":"799959613","g":1},{"in":["99953"],"out":"956332496","g":1},{"in":["27692"],"out":"960103823","g":1},{"in":["66564"],"out":"618035855","g":1},{"in":["78924"],"out":"187535939","g":1},{"in":["31655"],"out":"343479304","g":1},{"in":["98029"],"out":"986438633","g":1},{"in":["91273"],"out":"434272944","g":1},{"in":["50299"],"out":"323540523","g":1},{"in":["56837"],"out":"922918326","g":1},{"in":["24788"],"out":"614865262","g":1},{"in":["17192"],"out":"368770999","g":1},{"in":["99999"],"out":"816671055","g":1},{"in":["5"],"out":"94","g":1},{"in":["54222"],"out":"350411254","g":1},{"in":["98248"],"out":"135104707","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"An attendance record is a string of length `n` using `A` (absent), `L` (late) and `P` (present). A record is eligible for an award if it has fewer than 2 `A`s in total and never has 3 or more consecutive `L`s.\n\nReturn the number of eligible records of length `n`, modulo `10^9 + 7`.","constraints":["1 <= n <= 1e5"],"hints":["A record is described well enough by two numbers: how many A's so far (0 or 1), and how many L's at the very end (0, 1 or 2).","That is 6 states. Appending P, A or L moves between them: P resets the trailing Ls, A requires 0 A's so far, L requires fewer than 2 trailing Ls.","Update the 6 counts n times, modulo 10⁹ + 7, and add them up. Matrix exponentiation would make it O(log n)."],"explain":"There are 9 records of length 2 using P, A and L. Only \"AA\" breaks the rules (two absences), so 8 are eligible."},
{"slug":"beautiful-arrangement","title":"Beautiful Arrangement","level":"Medium","summary":"Count permutations of 1..n where, at every 1-indexed position i, perm[i] is divisible by i or i is divisible by perm[i].","method":"countArrangement","params":[["int","n"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["2"],"out":"2"},{"in":["1"],"out":"1"},{"in":["3"],"out":"3"},{"in":["6"],"out":"36"},{"in":["15"],"out":"24679"},{"in":["4"],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["5"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["7"],"out":"41","g":1},{"in":["8"],"out":"132","g":1},{"in":["9"],"out":"250","g":1},{"in":["10"],"out":"700","g":1},{"in":["11"],"out":"750","g":1},{"in":["12"],"out":"4010","g":1},{"in":["13"],"out":"4237","g":1},{"in":["14"],"out":"10680","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"A permutation `perm` of the numbers `1` to `n` is beautiful if, for every position `i` (1-indexed), `perm[i]` is divisible by `i` or `i` is divisible by `perm[i]`.\n\nReturn the number of beautiful permutations.","constraints":["1 <= n <= 15"],"hints":["Build the permutation position by position and prune as soon as a placement breaks the rule.","Backtracking with a \"used\" array is fast enough for n ≤ 15.","For a DP version, let the state be the set of numbers used (a bit mask). The next position is the count of bits set plus 1."],"explain":"Both orders of 1 and 2 work: in `[1,2]` each number equals its position, and in `[2,1]` 2 is divisible by position 1 and position 2 is divisible by 1. So there are 2 arrangements."},
{"slug":"partition-to-k-equal-sum-subsets","title":"Partition to K Equal Sum Subsets","level":"Medium","summary":"Return whether the array can be split into k non-empty subsets with equal sums.","method":"canPartitionKSubsets","params":[["int[]","nums"],["int","k"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["[4,3,2,3,5,2,1]","4"],"out":"true"},{"in":["[1,2,3,4]","3"],"out":"false"},{"in":["[5]","1"],"out":"true"},{"in":["[2,2,2,2,3,4,5]","4"],"out":"false"},{"in":["[1,1,1,1,2,2,2,2]","4"],"out":"true"},{"in":["[1]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[673,584,1887]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[2]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[169,20,434,101,128,312]","2"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[719,1086,719]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[5375,5379,5377,5379,5377,5378]","3"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[1,3,3,3,2,3,2,2,2,3]","6"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[2461,3413,133,13,3]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,2,3]","4"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[8]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[13,12,12,12,12,12,12,12]","8"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[3,1,3,3,3,3,2,3,3]","8"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[10000]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[5527,5527,5527,5527]","4"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,2,1,1]","2"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[7]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[2,2,1,1,1,3,2,1]","3"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[2,2,3,3,1,3,1,2,2]","2"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[6340,2061,8159,6002,10000,412,1,379,10000,4929,6111]","9"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[3900,3900,3900]","3"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,2,3,3,3,3,3,3,3]","9"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[6]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[3846,2,3517,344,12,428,87,32,272,1,1339]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[552,1335,1318]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[13,13,13,13,13,13,13]","7"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,5,3,4,2,1,3,1,2,4,3]","10"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[447]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1001,1155,4018]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[3121]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[9436,9436,9436,9436,9436,9436,9436]","7"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[12,12,12,12,12]","5"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,3]","2"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[3985,9047,5264,10000,10000,7014,1734]","4"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[3453]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[17]","1"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,1,1]","5"],"out":"true","g":1},{"in":["[3,2,3]","3"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[8441,8441,8441,8441,8441,8441,8441]","4"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[9883,1]","2"],"out":"false","g":1},{"in":["[3]","1"],"out":"true","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"Return `true` if the values of `nums` can be divided into `k` non-empty groups whose sums are all equal. Every value must be used exactly once.\n\nEvery group must reach exactly the total divided by `k`. If the total isn't divisible by `k`, or any value is larger than that target, the answer is `false` straight away.","constraints":["1 <= nums.length <= 16","1 <= k <= nums.length","1 <= nums[i] <= 1e4"],"hints":["Each group must sum to total / k. If that is not an integer, or some value is larger than it, return false.","Bit-mask DP: for each mask of used values, store the sum of the bucket currently being filled (total of mask modulo target). A value can be added if it fits in that bucket.","A backtracking alternative fills buckets one at a time, trying values in descending order and skipping equal choices."],"explain":"The total is 20, so each of the 4 groups must sum to 5: `(5)`, `(1,4)`, `(2,3)` and `(3,2)`. That works, so the answer is `true`."},
{"slug":"minimum-number-of-work-sessions-to-finish-the-tasks","title":"Minimum Number of Work Sessions to Finish the Tasks","level":"Medium","summary":"A work session lasts at most sessionTime hours and a task can't be split across sessions. Return the fewest sessions to finish every task (any order).","method":"minSessions","params":[["int[]","tasks"],["int","sessionTime"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[1,2,3]","3"],"out":"2"},{"in":["[3,1,3,1,1]","8"],"out":"2"},{"in":["[1,2,3,4,5]","15"],"out":"1"},{"in":["[5,5,5]","5"],"out":"3"},{"in":["[2,3,3,4,4,4,5,6,7,10]","12"],"out":"4"},{"in":["[2,3,1]","6"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[9,9,9,9]","13"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[5,5,5,10,10,10,10]","12"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,3,2,1]","9"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[8,9,7,1]","13"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[3,3,3,3,1,1,1]","7"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1]","15"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[1,2,1,1,1]","11"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[2,1,2,3,1,2,3,3,1,1,1,3]","10"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[3]","4"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[10,10,9,9,9,8,7,6,6,5,5]","15"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[3,3]","14"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[3]","9"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[3,3,2,2,1,3,1,3,1,2,1,1]","14"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[8]","13"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[3,3,3,2,1,1,1]","13"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[7,5,2,2,5,3]","14"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[3]","14"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[2,2,3,1,1,3,1,3]","13"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,7,1,7,7,7]","14"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[2,6,1,9,1,10,3,8,5,9]","13"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[3]","6"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1]","5"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[2,3,3,2,3,3,3,1,1]","12"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[4]","15"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,2,2,2,2,3,3,3]","7"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[3]","15"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[3,2]","10"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[5,4,4,3,2]","9"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[1]","4"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[9,9]","11"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[9,6]","13"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[7]","12"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[1,1,1,1,1,2,2,3,3,3,3,3,3,3]","4"],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["[7]","8"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[3,8,4,3]","9"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[1,3]","5"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[10,10,9,8,7,7,6,6,1,1,1]","13"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[1]","14"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[5,5]","6"],"out":"2","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"`tasks[i]` is the number of hours task `i` takes. You work in sessions of at most `sessionTime` hours each. A task must be finished within a single session, but you can do tasks in any order.\n\nReturn the minimum number of work sessions needed to finish all the tasks.","constraints":["1 <= tasks.length <= 14","1 <= tasks[i] <= 10","sessionTime <= 15","Every task fits in a session: max(tasks) ≤ sessionTime"],"hints":["With at most 14 tasks, you can afford a state that records which tasks are done: a bit mask.","For each mask, store the best pair (sessions used, hours used in the current session).","From a mask, add a task: if it fits in the current session, add its hours; otherwise start a new session. Keep the lexicographically smallest pair."],"explain":"Tasks 1 and 2 fit together in one 3-hour session and task 3 fills a second. One session can't hold all 6 hours, so the answer is 2."},
{"slug":"shortest-path-visiting-all-nodes","title":"Shortest Path Visiting All Nodes","level":"Hard","summary":"In a connected undirected graph (graph[i] lists i's neighbours), return the length of the shortest walk that visits every node. You may start and end anywhere and revisit nodes and edges.","method":"shortestPathLength","params":[["int[][]","graph"]],"returns":"int","tests":[{"in":["[[1,2,3],[0],[0],[0]]"],"out":"4"},{"in":["[[1],[0,2,4],[1,3,4],[2],[1,2]]"],"out":"4"},{"in":["[[]]"],"out":"0"},{"in":["[[1],[0,2],[1,3],[2]]"],"out":"3"},{"in":["[[4,5],[3,4,5],[3,4],[1,2],[0,1,2],[0,1]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[2,3],[3],[0],[0,1]]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[[4,8],[4,5,10],[6,7,9],[9],[0,1,6,8],[1],[2,4],[2],[0,4],[2,3],[1]]"],"out":"13","g":1},{"in":["[[1],[0]]"],"out":"1","g":1},{"in":["[[1],[0,2],[1,4,5],[4],[2,3],[2]]"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[[1,4,7],[0,3],[3,4,5,6,7],[1,2,4,7],[0,2,3,5],[2,4,7],[2,7],[0,2,3,5,6]]"],"out":"7","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,3],[0],[0,3],[0,2]]"],"out":"3","g":1},{"in":["[[1,3,5,7],[0,2],[1,6],[0,9],[9],[0,6],[2,5,8],[0,9],[6],[3,4,7]]"],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["[[3],[3,5],[4,8],[0,1,6,8],[2],[1],[3,7,8],[6],[2,3,6]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[1,4,5,6,8],[0,3,4,6,7],[3,4,5],[1,2,5,6],[0,1,2,5,8],[0,2,3,4],[0,1,3],[1],[0,4]]"],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["[[3],[2,4],[1,3],[0,2,4],[1,3]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,8,9],[0,3,7],[0,5,7,10],[1,4,9,10],[3,8,10],[2],[7,8,10],[1,2,6,10],[0,4,6,10],[0,3],[2,3,4,6,7,8]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,3,4],[0,2,3],[0,1,4],[0,1,4,5],[0,2,3,5],[3,4]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[5,8],[3],[4,6,9],[1,4],[2,3,5],[0,4,9],[2,8],[9],[0,6],[2,5,7]]"],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,3],[0,2,4],[0,1,5],[0],[1],[2]]"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[[4,5,6,8],[6],[5],[4,6],[0,3,5,9],[0,2,4],[0,1,3,7],[6],[0,9],[4,8]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[2,3,6,9],[4,8],[0,4,7],[0,4,5,7],[1,2,3,5,7],[3,4,8],[0],[2,3,4,8],[1,5,7],[0]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[4,8,9],[8],[4],[4],[0,2,3,6],[6,10],[4,5,7],[6],[0,1],[0],[5]]"],"out":"14","g":1},{"in":["[[3],[2],[1,3,4],[0,2],[2]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[1,3],[0,2,3,4],[1,4],[0,1,4],[1,2,3]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[2,4,5,8],[3,5,6,7,8,9],[0,4,9],[1,7],[0,2,8,9],[0,1,6,8],[1,5],[1,3,8],[0,1,4,5,7],[1,2,4]]"],"out":"9","g":1},{"in":["[[2],[2],[0,1]]"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,4,7,9,10],[0,8,9],[0,6,11],[10],[0],[6,7,8],[2,5,7,10,11],[0,5,6],[1,5,11],[0,1],[0,3,6],[2,6,8]]"],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2],[0,2],[0,1]]"],"out":"2","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2],[0,4,5],[0,3,4],[2],[1,2],[1]]"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[[2,3,4],[2,3],[0,1,4],[0,1],[0,2]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[4],[3],[3,4],[1,2,4],[0,2,3]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[1],[0,3,8],[6],[1,6,7],[5,6,8],[4,6,7],[2,3,4,5,8],[3,5],[1,4,6]]"],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["[[3,4],[2,4],[1],[0,5],[0,1],[3]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[9],[8],[3],[2,7],[7],[7,8,9],[7,9],[3,4,5,6],[1,5],[0,5,6]]"],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["[[3],[3,5],[3,4,5],[0,1,2,4,5],[2,3,5,6],[1,2,3,4],[4]]"],"out":"6","g":1},{"in":["[[2],[2],[0,1,3],[2]]"],"out":"4","g":1},{"in":["[[1,2,8],[0,2,3,5,7,8],[0,1,6],[1,6],[8,10],[1,7,10],[2,3,10],[1,5,8,9],[0,1,4,7,9],[7,8,10],[4,5,6,9]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[2,5,6,8,9],[2,4,8],[0,1],[5,8,10],[1,6,10],[0,3],[0,4,7,8],[6,10],[0,1,3,6,10],[0],[3,4,7,8]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[5],[4,5],[3],[2,4,6,7],[1,3,7],[0,1,6],[3,5],[3,4]]"],"out":"8","g":1},{"in":["[[1,5,10],[0,4],[3,7,9],[2,9],[1,6,9],[0,8],[4],[2],[5],[2,3,4],[0]]"],"out":"12","g":1},{"in":["[[5],[5,6],[3,4,9],[2,7],[2],[0,1,6,8,9],[1,5,8,9],[3],[5,6],[2,5,6]]"],"out":"11","g":1},{"in":["[[4],[2],[1,3,4],[2],[0,2]]"],"out":"5","g":1},{"in":["[[1,4,9],[0,2,4,6],[1,3],[2],[0,1,6,7,9],[8,9],[1,4,9],[4],[5],[0,4,5,6]]"],"out":"10","g":1},{"in":["[[2,4,6],[3,5,6,8],[0,3,7,9],[1,2,7,8,9],[0,6,8],[1],[0,1,4,7,8,9],[2,3,6],[1,3,4,6],[2,3,6]]"],"out":"9","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"`graph` is a connected undirected graph with `n` nodes, where `graph[i]` lists the neighbours of node `i`. Return the length (number of edges) of the shortest walk that visits every node.\n\nYou may start and end at any node, and you may revisit nodes and reuse edges.","constraints":["1 <= graph.length <= 12","0 <= graph[i][j] < graph.length","The graph is connected and has no self-loops"],"hints":["The position alone is not enough as a state: you also need to know which nodes have been visited.","Run BFS over states (node, mask of visited nodes), starting from every (i, 1 << i) at once.","The first time you reach a state whose mask has every bit set, its distance is the answer."],"explain":"Node 0 is connected to 1, 2 and 3. The walk 1 → 0 → 2 → 0 → 3 visits every node in 4 moves (revisiting 0 is allowed), and no shorter walk does. So the answer is 4."},
