"ababbabb\"]"],"out":"\"aabbbbbabbbaababbabbaabbba\"","g":1}],"lesson":"dp-state-machine","statement":"Return a shortest string that contains every string in `words` as a substring. No word is a substring of another.\n\nIf several shortest strings exist, any of them is accepted.\n\nWhen one word ends with the start of another, the two can share those letters, which shortens the result. Here no such overlap exists.","constraints":["1 <= words.length <= 12","1 <= words[i].length <= 20","Words are lowercase and unique","No word is a substring of another"],"hints":["Placing word b right after word a saves the length of the longest suffix of a that is a prefix of b. Precompute that overlap for every pair.","The task becomes finding the order of words that maximises the total overlap: a travelling-salesman style problem.","DP over (mask of words used, last word) storing the best total overlap and the parent choice, then rebuild the string by following the parents."],"explain":"None of the words overlap, so a shortest superstring simply joins all three: 4 + 5 + 8 = 17 characters, for example \"leetcodelovesalex\". Any other order of the same length is also accepted."}
